# The 0061 and 0062 migration steps for .github/workflows/ci.yml
#
# WHY THIS IS A PATCH AND NOT A COMMIT: the GitHub App has NO workflow
# scope, and GitHub refuses the push outright:
#
#   "refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update workflow
#    .github/workflows/ci.yml without `workflows` permission"
#
# This is the standing rule -- the owner applies workflow changes.
#
# APPLY IT WITH:
#
#   git apply docs/ci-ingredient-aliases-0061-0062.patch
#
# NOTE: if you already applied docs/ci-ingredient-aliases-0061.patch
# (from the 0061 PR), skip the 0061 block below and apply only the
# 0062 block. Applying this patch on top of that one will conflict.
#
# WHY IT IS NEEDED: the migration-chain validator compares three lists --
# .github/workflows/ci.yml (the CI database), scripts/ci-migration-chain.sh
# (the Nightly database) and scripts/repro-ci-db.sh (the LOCAL
# reproduction). These PRs added 0061 and 0062 to the two scripts. The
# workflow is the third list, and it cannot be pushed by the App, so it
# has to be patched. Without it the validator fails with:
#
#   CI migration chain MISMATCH:
#   in scripts/ci-migration-chain.sh but NOT in .github/workflows/ci.yml:
#   db/migrations/0061_ingredient_aliases.sql
#   db/migrations/0062_ingredients_sourcing_vocabulary.sql
#
# A migration that is not applied is a schema that does not exist, and the
# route that reads it returns 500. The local reproduction drifting from
# CI is how a developer ends up debugging a failure that the CI database
# does not have.
#
# WHERE THEY GO: the two steps run immediately after 0060 (the legacy
# associations, published as Unverified) and before the PER-DISH backfill
# assertions, which must stay LAST because they assert the state the
# whole chain produces.
#
# Generated against main at 7c0c53c (the merge of PR #262, WP-C1).
# The patch applies cleanly to that tree.
#
diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 7244091..9fb6c56 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -1338,6 +1338,31 @@ jobs:
             -f db/migrations/0060_legacy_associations_published.sql 2>&1 | tee /tmp/m0060.log
           bash scripts/check-ci-markers.sh "the legacy associations, published as Unverified" "0060: ok" /tmp/m0060.log
 
+      # ── 0061: the ingredient aliases table ────────────────────────────
+      #
+      # The ingredient alias table. A RETIRED ingredient slug that must
+      # keep resolving, mapped to the canonical ingredient -- so a merge
+      # of two duplicates does not break the retired URL.
+      #
+      # It is additive: a table of alternative names for an ingredient. It
+      # publishes nothing.
+      - name: Apply the ingredient aliases table
+        run: |
+          PGPASSWORD=gustale psql -h 127.0.0.1 -U postgres -d gustale_ci -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 \
+            -f db/migrations/0061_ingredient_aliases.sql 2>&1 | tee /tmp/m0061.log
+          bash scripts/check-ci-markers.sh "the ingredient aliases table" "INGREDIENT_ALIASES_OK" /tmp/m0061.log
+
+      # ── 0062: the ingredient sourcing vocabulary ───────────────────────
+      #
+      # Migration 0062 adds the 21 reviewed ingredient rows (GUS-1108) --
+      # the vocabulary the sourcing availability rows attach to. It is
+      # additive and publishes nothing.
+      - name: Apply the ingredient sourcing vocabulary
+        run: |
+          PGPASSWORD=gustale psql -h 127.0.0.1 -U postgres -d gustale_ci -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 \
+            -f db/migrations/0062_ingredients_sourcing_vocabulary.sql 2>&1 | tee /tmp/m0062.log
+          bash scripts/check-ci-markers.sh "the ingredient sourcing vocabulary" "0062: all 6 proofs passed" /tmp/m0062.log
+
       # The PER-DISH backfill assertions. LAST, because they assert the
       # state the whole chain produces: the reference dishes'
       # association rows AND the journey places in the editorial queue.
